  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the extracted `composerPrefill.ts`/`launchCreate.ts`/`attachmentsSource.ts`, when grepped, then none contains `import ... from 'react'`, any React runtime API, or an `as React.ComponentType` cast (React-agnostic Layer-1, NFR-05).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the `CommunicationActions` PCF, when built with `npm run build:prod`, then it compiles clean importing the three logic modules from `@spaarke/communication-components`, its local duplicates are deleted, and its React 16 view is unchanged (regression-free, NFR-04).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `deriveComposerFields` in Reply / Reply All / Forward mode, when invoked on a record, then recipients + subject ("Re:"/"Fwd:") + quoted-thread body are derived identically to pre-extraction (feeds FR-09 reader-pane compose without forking the composer).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a create-from-email action, when `launchCreate` runs, then it opens the OOB `Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo` modal for the correct target (`CREATE_LAUNCH_TARGETS`: event/todo/invoice) — contract unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the shared barrel, when imported, then it re-exports the actions logic without disturbing the connections (020) / attachments (021) exports; no business logic duplicated between PCF and shared lib.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the extracted logic does NOT construct or fork a composer — grep confirms no new composer component; it only computes `ComposerFields` consumed by the canonical `SendEmailPage`/`EmailComposer`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Shared lib build + PCF `build:prod` both green; existing `CommunicationActions` unit tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Cite spec FR-18 + FR-08 + NFR-04 + NFR-05 in the PR. EXTRACTION of existing code (COMPLETE-class) — no §11 `&lt;justification&gt;` (modify/refactor exempt). Barrel edits serialize with 021 — coordinate the `src/index.ts` edit. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `@spaarke/communication-components`, contended with messaging-r2/r3, notification-spine-r1, email-r4). Completion summary appended here when done.</notes>

